                  "explanation": "Wernicke (1874) localized language comprehension to the posterior superior temporal gyrus of the left hemisphere. Lesions here produce **Wernicke's aphasia**: fluent but meaningless speech with impaired comprehension. Broca's aphasia is the opposite picture (non-fluent, effortful, but comprehension preserved). Heschl's gyrus damage causes auditory deficits, not language deficits, because primary auditory processing precedes language interpretation.",
